# Shell scripts MUST be LF, always, on every platform.
#
# A script checked out with CRLF has `#!/bin/sh\r` as its shebang. Linux then looks for
# an interpreter literally named `/bin/sh\r`, does not find one, and reports
# "no such file or directory" — naming the script, not the interpreter, so it reads as
# though the file is missing when it is sitting right there.
#
# That is not hypothetical: docker/migrate-entrypoint.sh was committed with CRLF, which
# made the `migrator` image unrunnable from any Windows clone. Migrations are the one
# thing that has to work before anything else does.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else read by a Linux interpreter or an init hook.
docker/**/*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/**/*.sh text eol=lf
